  "prefLabel": "Plc 1404.05 Processing of Applications for Initial Licensure; Decisions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1404.05 Processing of Applications for Initial Licensure; Decisions.\n\n(a) Within 30 days of receipt of an application for initial licensure submitted pursuant to Plc 1404.02, the licensing bureau shall process the application as provided in Plc 304.06.\n\n(b) The application shall be subject to the abandonment provisions of Plc 304.06(h) and the withdrawal provisions of Plc 304.07.\n\n(c) After determining that an application is complete, the licensing bureau shall review the application in accordance with Plc 304.08.\n\n(d) The licensing bureau shall make a decision and notify the applicant in accordance with Plc 304.09, subject to (e), below.\n\n(e) The licensing bureau shall approve an application for initial licensure and issue a license to practice recreational therapy if the applicant:\n\n(1) Has submitted an application that meets the requirements of Plc 1404.02;\n\n(2) Has demonstrated good moral character in the answers to the background and character questions in Plc 304.03(e) and any explanations provided pursuant to Plc 304.04; and\n\n(3) Meets all statutory requirements, as restated in Plc 1404.01.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1400) #13705, eff 8-1-23; ss by #14442, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES 1-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1400.html"
